WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.202
-Priyanka, have you ever
seen the show on YouTube

00:00:03.202 --> 00:00:05.304
called "Hot Ones"?
-Yes, I have.

00:00:05.304 --> 00:00:07.573
He almost killed my husband.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:07.573 --> 00:00:10.376
-You eat spicy chicken wings
that get hotter and hotter

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:13.379
as you go, all while answering
questions about yourself.

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:15.014
-Okay.
-Do you wanna try it right now?

00:00:15.014 --> 00:00:16.949
-Yeah, why do we do this?
-I don't know why.

00:00:16.949 --> 00:00:18.584
-Why do we do this to ourselves?
-I'm already getting --

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:20.519
I'm already freaking out.
-I mean, I love spice,

00:00:20.519 --> 00:00:22.655
but I'm just, like,
the escalation of it

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:24.924
is making me nervous.
-And he's the best guy to do it.

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:26.359
Ladies and gentlemen,
give it up for the host

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:28.294
of "Hot Ones,"
Sean Evans, right there.

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:29.829
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:31.998
The maestro.

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:33.233
-Okay.

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:35.334
-Jimmy, thank you so much
for having me back.

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:36.836
Priyanka, it is an honor.

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:38.304
And for those
who are unfamiliar,

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:40.106
"Hot Ones," it's really simple.

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:42.275
We have these wings.
We have an interview.

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:44.610
And we'll start here
in a Chill Zone and then quickly

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:48.815
work our way up to a hot sauce,
the Last Dab Triple-X --

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:52.218
more than 400 times hotter
than a jalapeño.

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:53.552
-What?
[ Audience groans ]

00:00:53.552 --> 00:00:54.754
-Gosh.
-But --

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:56.655
-400, with two zeros.
-400.

00:00:56.655 --> 00:00:59.859
400. But this first one
is a nice Chill Zone.

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:01.193
Los Calientes.

00:01:01.193 --> 00:01:02.328
-Which one?
This one or that one?

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:04.097
-Start right there
at the handle there.

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:05.398
There we go.
-This is it here.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:08.067
Los Calientes, okay?
That's this one.

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:11.938
-Nothing to fear.
4 out of 10 on our heat index.

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:14.407
-Mm-hmm, okay.

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:15.841
-It's okay.
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:15.841 --> 00:01:18.511
-Good, too.
Okay.

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:19.979
-And, Jimmy,
I want to start with you,

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:22.281
because recently, we had
Ashton Kutcher on the show.

00:01:22.281 --> 00:01:23.816
-Mm-hmm.
-And he told us this story

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:25.451
about having
to go to the hospital

00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:28.321
because he was experimenting
with this Steve Jobs diet

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:30.156
where he only eats fruit.
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:32.725
-What can you tell people
about the "Cape Fear" diet,

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:34.861
where you just eat
turkey on toast,

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:36.663
and what are its consequences?

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:39.765
-I did this in college.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.765 --> 00:01:41.867
Spitting because it's so hot.
I did it on college.

00:01:41.867 --> 00:01:44.370
I just ate a turkey sandwich
for breakfast, lunch, and dinner

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:47.273
for like four or five days,
and it was a disaster.

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:48.474
I don't know why I did it.

00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:50.276
I heard that De Niro did it
in "Cape Fear,"

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:52.712
and so I just did it
to try to get in shape,

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.547
and it was awful.
-Did it work?

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:56.282
-I didn't really
need to lose weight.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:57.984
I was skinny, anyway,
but I just started

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:59.251
getting mad at people,
and I was getting angry.

00:01:59.251 --> 00:02:01.720
-Yeah, I get really mad.
-Well, I wonder what

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:03.956
I have in store,
eating these wings of death

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:05.324
for the past four years.

00:02:05.324 --> 00:02:10.562
But let's move on here to
Bravado Spice Co's Aka Miso.

00:02:10.562 --> 00:02:12.498
We have ghost pepper,

00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:14.534
and we also have Carolina Reaper
in this one,

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:16.369
all in one condiment.
-Carolina Reaper?

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:18.404
I don't even know --
These are names of peppers?

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:20.440
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:21.640
Okay.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:22.909
All right.

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:24.177
That's a little something,
right?

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:27.180
-Yeah, I feel a kick.
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.581
-But doable.
-It's doable?

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:29.815
-All right.

00:02:29.815 --> 00:02:32.018
-Priyanka, we're gonna
shift the focus to you,

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:33.653
because in our
season 9 premiere,

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:35.821
we featured the Jonas Brothers.
-Uh-huh, uh-huh.

00:02:35.821 --> 00:02:38.758
-And then, Nick said that
you gave him a pep talk

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:40.659
before his date
with the wings of death.

00:02:40.659 --> 00:02:42.061
Do you remember
what you told him

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:45.031
about the perils
of eating spicy food?

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:47.367
And did he have any kind of
reaction afterwards?

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.301
-Well, I did tell him
that he needs to do this

00:02:49.301 --> 00:02:51.237
for the Indians,
now that he's married to...

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:52.639
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:55.140
...now that he's married
to my entire country,

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:58.945
that he needs to, like,
bring it home for us.

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:00.847
So he, like,
really tried to get it.

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:02.115
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.115 --> 00:03:04.650
But after your show,
it was a long conversation.

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:05.784
And a brutal three days --
-Why are you not eating --

00:03:05.784 --> 00:03:06.952
Why are you not eating
your chicken wing?

00:03:06.952 --> 00:03:08.521
-Oh.
Because I'm talking.

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:10.256
-Oh, my gosh.
Oh, my gosh.

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:11.757
Oh, my gosh.

00:03:11.757 --> 00:03:12.825
All right.
Oh, my gosh.

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:14.093
-All right.
Well, you know what?

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:16.595
I hope he did you proud.
He did us proud.

00:03:16.595 --> 00:03:19.732
-He did me very proud.
-And here, we are moving on

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:22.268
to Da Bomb, a sauce Jimmy
knows all too well,

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:23.869
a sauce I know all too well.

00:03:23.869 --> 00:03:26.072
I apologize in advance,
Priyanka.

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:27.473
-I don't like --
[ Clears throat ]

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:29.374
[ Laughter ]
[ Coughing ]

00:03:29.374 --> 00:03:30.543
I don't like Da Bomb.

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:33.279
That what killed me
last time I did this.

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:36.082
Are you feeling something?
-Yeah, I feel it, I feel it.

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:38.518
-Well, get ready,
because Da Bomb is da worst.

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:40.386
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:41.554
All right, here we go.
-Here we go.

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:42.755
-Just do it fast, all right?
-Okay.

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:46.025
-All right.
Oh, my gosh.

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:48.160
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:49.662
-Oh, I feel it.
Mm-hmm.

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:51.597
-That is the worst.
-All right.

00:03:51.597 --> 00:03:52.731
Anyone who watches
"Hot Ones" knows...

00:03:52.731 --> 00:03:54.600
-Whoo!
-It sneaks up on you.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.001
-...that we have
a recurring segment called

00:03:56.001 --> 00:03:57.369
"Explain that Gram,"

00:03:57.369 --> 00:04:00.906
and here, we have pulled
a great Jimmy Fallon throwback.

00:04:00.906 --> 00:04:02.709
Let's put it up on the monitor.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:03.943
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:05.478
-Jimmy Fallon and Jay Z.

00:04:05.478 --> 00:04:08.080
Priyanka, can you guess
what they were talking about?

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.082
And then, Jimmy, can you
set the record straight?

00:04:10.082 --> 00:04:12.451
-I think Jay Z is trying
to buy the Fallon show.

00:04:12.451 --> 00:04:15.188
The Jimmy Fallon show,
and he's discovering --

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:17.456
he's discussing how much
he's gonna get paid for it.

00:04:17.456 --> 00:04:19.992
That's why he looks so happy.

00:04:19.992 --> 00:04:21.393
-That's the weirdest photo
I've ever seen.

00:04:21.393 --> 00:04:22.861
Um...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.861 --> 00:04:25.464
I think I'm explaining to him
how weird my shirt is.

00:04:25.464 --> 00:04:28.100
It's a very odd shirt.
Like, look at the pocket.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:29.435
The stripes
are going the wrong way.

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:31.303
-Oh, my gosh.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.303 --> 00:04:32.671
-Where was I?
What shirt was that?

00:04:32.671 --> 00:04:35.475
Oh, my God.
-A timeless shirt.

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:37.910
-Aah!
-A timeless collar.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:40.613
This is the Last Dab.
We call it the Last Dab,

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:42.582
because it's tradition
around here

00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:43.983
to put a little extra
on the last wing.

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:45.117
-This hurts.

00:04:45.117 --> 00:04:46.685
-You don't have to
if you don't want to.

00:04:46.685 --> 00:04:47.820
-I'm shak--
My hands are shaking.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.655
I really -- Look at this,
look at this.

00:04:49.655 --> 00:04:50.989
My hands are shaking.
I can't stop shaking.

00:04:50.989 --> 00:04:52.258
-You don't have to
if you don't want to.

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:54.294
-Why do we do this to ourselves?
-Oh, my gosh, Sean.

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:56.896
-Stay calm, stay calm.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:04:56.896 --> 00:04:59.165
All right, I'm gonna do a dab.
I have to, right?

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:05.904
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:05.904 --> 00:05:08.407
Aah!
Aah!

00:05:08.407 --> 00:05:12.078
Oh, my God.
-All right.

00:05:12.078 --> 00:05:14.547
Taking a lap, taking a lap.

00:05:14.547 --> 00:05:17.082
Surviving the "Hot Ones"
experience.

00:05:17.082 --> 00:05:18.884
-All right.
-I'm crying!

00:05:18.884 --> 00:05:19.985
-Oh, I'm crying, dude.

00:05:19.985 --> 00:05:21.787
[ Laughter ]
Oh, my God.

00:05:21.787 --> 00:05:24.123
-All right.
Bottoms up.

00:05:24.123 --> 00:05:26.258
-Sean Evans, you are insane.
All right, here we go.

00:05:26.258 --> 00:05:28.127
-How do you do this every day?

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:30.630
♪♪

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.498
-All right.

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:37.903
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:37.903 --> 00:05:39.272
All right.

00:05:39.272 --> 00:05:41.306
Here we are
at the end of the line.

00:05:41.306 --> 00:05:44.677
And, Jimmy, last time we played
a "Name That Impression" game,

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:47.913
and here we're gonna stay with
that theme, but it's on music.

00:05:47.913 --> 00:05:49.415
I want you
to think about the first...

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:51.016
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.016 --> 00:05:54.987
...musical impression that comes
to mind with your mouth on fire,

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:57.923
tongue ablaze, throat singed,

00:05:57.923 --> 00:05:59.692
sing the first one
that comes to mind.

00:05:59.692 --> 00:06:01.060
Priyanka,
try to guess the singer.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:02.261
-What are you saying?
What, what?

00:06:02.261 --> 00:06:03.896
-Musical impression.
Musical impression.

00:06:03.896 --> 00:06:05.330
-What about musical impressions?
What?

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:07.766
-The first one that comes
to mind, just sing something.

00:06:07.766 --> 00:06:10.002
-Aah!
I have to sing a song?

00:06:10.002 --> 00:06:11.570
-Yes.
-Uh, uh, um...

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:14.807
I can't think of a song.
I can't think of a song.

00:06:14.807 --> 00:06:17.076
♪♪

00:06:17.076 --> 00:06:19.679
♪ Happy birthday to you,
happy birthday to you ♪

00:06:19.679 --> 00:06:20.813
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

00:06:20.813 --> 00:06:22.681
Oh, I have to do
an impression of somebody?

00:06:22.681 --> 00:06:24.050
Oh.

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:26.618
♪ Well, you can tell
by the way I use my walk ♪

00:06:26.618 --> 00:06:29.055
♪ I'm a woman's man,
no time to talk ♪

00:06:29.055 --> 00:06:30.356
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:30.356 --> 00:06:33.325
-That would be The Bee Gees.
Let's make some noise!

00:06:33.325 --> 00:06:34.327
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:34.327 --> 00:06:37.963
For Jimmy Fallon,
Priyanka Chopra.

00:06:37.963 --> 00:06:40.199
-That's Sean Evans!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:42.668
How you doing?
-I can't talk.

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:44.804
-More "Tonight Show"
after the break, everybody.

00:06:44.804 --> 00:06:46.572
Oh, my God.

